# Git for Windows' core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check files out with
# CRLF line endings. That breaks shell scripts under bash (macOS, Linux,
# WSL), and makes `gofmt -l .` list every Go file (CLAUDE.md requires it to
# print nothing). The repository itself stores LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
